 "input": "how the exam board marks papers. scripts are scanned after the exam and split into question items in the marking system. senior examiners write the mark scheme and pick seed scripts. examiners do standardisation: mark practice scripts and must be within tolerance before live marking. seed scripts are slipped into live marking to keep checking examiners, ones who drift get stopped. marks go into the results database. grade boundaries set by the awarding committee looking at statistics and scripts. results day, then schools can ask for reviews of marking, which re-mark against the same mark scheme.",
